<h1>TActiveRatingList</h1>
<com:SinceVersion Version="3.1" />
<com:DocLink ClassPath="Prado.Web.UI.ActiveControls.TActiveRatingList" />

<p class="block-content">
<tt>TActiveRatingList</tt> is the active counterpart to the original <tt>TRatingList</tt> control.
</p>

<p class="block-content">
The <tt>AutoPostBack</tt> property is set to true by default.
Thus, when a radio button is clicked a <tt>OnCallback</tt> event is
raised after <tt>OnSelectedIndexChanged</tt> event.
</p>

<h2>What updates during a callback</h2>

<p class="block-content">
The selection can be changed from the server. Assigning <tt>SelectedIndex</tt>,
<tt>SelectedIndices</tt>, <tt>SelectedValue</tt>, or <tt>SelectedValues</tt> moves the
selection in the browser, subject to <a href="?page=ActiveControls.Introduction#ClientSideUpdates">the five conditions for a client-side update</a>. A list with a prompt item counts
the prompt outside the index, in the same way a postback does.
</p>

<h2>Rating properties</h2>

<table class="parameters">
<tr><th>Property</th><th>Effect during a callback</th></tr>
<tr>
	<td><tt>Rating</tt></td>
	<td>Sets how many stars are filled, including a half star where <tt>HalfRatingInterval</tt> allows one.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
	<td><tt>Caption</tt></td>
	<td>Replaces the text shown beside the stars.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
	<td><tt>ReadOnly</tt></td>
	<td>Stops or allows further rating by the user.</td>
</tr>
</table>

<p class="block-content">
Each of the three reaches the browser by calling into the control's client script, subject
to <a href="?page=ActiveControls.Introduction#ClientSideUpdates">the five conditions for a client-side update</a>.
</p>

<h2>The items are fixed</h2>

<p class="block-content">
The <tt>Items</tt> collection cannot be rebuilt during a callback. Set the number of stars
before the control renders.
</p>

<p class="block-content">
Please refer to the original documentation of <a href="?page=Controls.List">TRatingList</a> for usage.
</p>

